      'Rule example: Be the first to collect 15 or more wu (winning cards) and declare a win (食湖 sik wu).',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Optional: Any player with a supreme combination (cards 2-4 and 1-2, at least one of each) may lay it face up; it counts as wu.\n2. Dealer leads any card or valid combination face up.\n3. In turn each player may beat the current play with a higher card or combination of the same count and suit mix, or pass.\n4. When all but one pass in succession, that player takes the winning cards as wu and leads next.\n5. First to have 15 or more wu may declare (sik wu); play ends and winner receives chip payments: 1 chip for 15-17 wu, 2 for 18-20, up to 5 for 27-28. A player may delay declaring to try for more wu but then must reach the next threshold to declare.',
